It may be a Slash'em specific thing (I don't thing so) but shopkeepers do  
pay something for any un-ided gems. Not much, but something around 4 or 6  
zormkids per gem. They don't pay anything for identified glass, but  
unicorn-ided is not considered ided by the game and so they do pay as for  
any unided gem.

Of course, that's completely worthless for real gems where the real price  
is much higher, but for glass, it can be a little useful. Especially since  
by the time I find unicorn for pseudo-iding, I usually find a general shop  
(Minetown) and I need the money (because I'm not always strong enough to  
handle all the monsters generated while shoplifting). And at that moment,  
it is sometime possible to have a total of more or less 40 different  
glasses, making for a nice enough sum of money.

I usually stop taking glass after that, unless I really really need the  
few extra zormkids.

